                "img": "https://arxiv.org/html/2611.21938/2611.21938v1/figures/seq22/s0.jpg",
                "caption": "Fig. 6:One episode of HubEgo-100K (14.8 minutes), a watch movement assembly at a watchmaker’s bench, with video, sensors and annotations on one timeline. Top: six frames with their time in the episode. Middle: the native accelerometer and gyroscope streams (min-max envelope of the 88,864 samples of each stream; dashed lines mark the six frames) and a 0.2-second window with the capture times of the video frames, the native accelerometer samples and the value at each frame time by linear interpolation, the method of the per-frame readings. Bottom: the released annotations. By model estimate, at least one hand appears in 99.8% of the sampled frames and both hands in 90.3%, and the on-task share is 99.7%.",
